WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.867
- I was 11 years old when I
put myself into foster care.

00:00:02.867 --> 00:00:06.034
(slow dramatic music)

00:00:07.803 --> 00:00:10.574
It kind of came to a breaking
point around when I turned 11.

00:00:10.574 --> 00:00:12.233
There was a lot of physical fights,

00:00:12.233 --> 00:00:13.823
there was a lot of just emotional abuse.

00:00:13.823 --> 00:00:15.288
I just kept having issues with my dad.

00:00:15.288 --> 00:00:17.575
We never got along,
we'd always butt heads,

00:00:17.575 --> 00:00:19.879
and then he started dating his cousin

00:00:19.879 --> 00:00:22.191
which was a little weird for me.

00:00:22.191 --> 00:00:23.852
I ended up calling the Kids Help Phone.

00:00:23.852 --> 00:00:26.148
I told them that I was depressed,

00:00:26.148 --> 00:00:28.764
that I'm having all
these issues in my home

00:00:28.764 --> 00:00:30.852
and that I couldn't take it
anymore and I needed to get out.

00:00:30.852 --> 00:00:33.723
Then the police came and
then I got taken away

00:00:33.723 --> 00:00:34.939
and put into foster care.

00:00:34.939 --> 00:00:36.658
I first went into a girls home.

00:00:36.658 --> 00:00:38.598
I feel like we should take
home out of girls home.

00:00:38.598 --> 00:00:41.270
My stuff would get stolen all
the time, I would get beat up.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:44.904
I ended up at a cucumber
farm with Mennonites.

00:00:44.904 --> 00:00:48.103
I ended up with a very,
very religious family.

00:00:48.103 --> 00:00:51.253
It felt like I was just sort
of an extra in their movie.

00:00:51.253 --> 00:00:53.115
I was just like an extra in their life.

00:00:53.115 --> 00:00:54.440
I ended up at a bunch of different homes

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:56.347
but I didn't find anything very permanent.

00:00:56.347 --> 00:00:57.815
There was really nowhere to go.

00:00:57.815 --> 00:01:00.395
I moved out just before I turned 17.

00:01:00.395 --> 00:01:03.662
I was in high school and
I was working full time.

00:01:03.662 --> 00:01:05.563
I still had a little
bit of monthly support

00:01:05.563 --> 00:01:07.819
from the children's aid,
but as soon as I turned 21,

00:01:07.819 --> 00:01:09.945
they cut off all benefits.

00:01:09.945 --> 00:01:11.941
I lost everything I had.

00:01:11.941 --> 00:01:15.108
(slow dramatic music)

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:23.574
You're just starting one of
the biggest parts of your life

00:01:23.574 --> 00:01:27.661
and then now you're just shoved
to the side and unimportant.

00:01:27.661 --> 00:01:30.281
I remember repeatedly going into

00:01:30.281 --> 00:01:32.521
negative in my bank account.

00:01:32.521 --> 00:01:34.468
I'd just paid my rent and then

00:01:34.468 --> 00:01:36.006
I didn't have any money for food.

00:01:36.006 --> 00:01:38.093
I couldn't afford toilet paper.

00:01:38.093 --> 00:01:41.176
(upbeat dance music)

00:01:54.421 --> 00:01:57.052
I feel like youth who are
aging out of foster care,

00:01:57.052 --> 00:01:59.584
they don't have the financial training.

00:01:59.584 --> 00:02:01.587
They don't have the emotional support

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:04.481
and it's a no wonder
they're ending up homeless

00:02:04.481 --> 00:02:06.718
and they're ending up
not grading high school,

00:02:06.718 --> 00:02:08.946
not going to college, not
getting a proper education

00:02:08.946 --> 00:02:10.642
and ending up broke.

00:02:10.642 --> 00:02:13.725
(upbeat dance music)

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:25.700
What up, foxx family?

00:02:38.264 --> 00:02:40.440
I just think that if there's
anyone going through this,

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.623
like anyone that's going
through being a youth

00:02:42.623 --> 00:02:44.108
that's about to age out of foster care,

00:02:44.108 --> 00:02:45.691
that's aging out of foster care,

00:02:45.691 --> 00:02:48.254
there is thousands of other people

00:02:48.254 --> 00:02:50.136
that are going through
the same thing as you.

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:51.454
You're not alone.

00:02:51.454 --> 00:02:54.537
(upbeat dance music)

